        "inventory.item__t": {
            "preferredApproach": [
                "item__t has 10M+ rows. Available indexes: item__t_id_idx (id), item__t___id_idx (__id), idx_item_holdings_material (holdings_record_id, material_type_id).",
                "ALWAYS access items through holdings_record_id to use the composite index. Never scan item__t first and join back to holdings.",
                "There is NO index on effective_location_id. For location-based queries, scope through holdings permanent_location_id first, then check items.",
                "For material type filtering, use the composite index: WHERE ii.holdings_record_id = hr.id AND ii.material_type_id = <uuid>.",
                "Use nested EXISTS from holdings to items: EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM inventory.item__t ii WHERE ii.holdings_record_id = hr.id AND ii.material_type_id = ...).",
                "Use inventory.item__t for current item status and availability snapshots; use circulation tables for loan events."
            ]
        },
        "inventory.instance__t": {
            "preferredApproach": [
                "Use inventory.instance__t as the bibliographic anchor for title-level inventory queries.",
                "Join to holdings via holdings_record__t.instance_id = instance__t.id, then to items via item__t.holdings_record_id = holdings_record__t.id.",
                "For MARC field-level extraction, prefer folio_source_record.marctab instead of parsing source-record JSON text.",
                "For full MARC record output, ALWAYS include folio_source_record.records__t.parsed_record__content joined via records__t.external_id = instance__t.id AND records__t.state = 'ACTUAL'.",
                "PERFORMANCE: When building instance-level CTEs with item-level filters (material type, item status), ALWAYS use nested EXISTS with AS MATERIALIZED. Never use JOIN + DISTINCT.",
                "PERFORMANCE: Resolve material_type_id via scalar subquery: ii.material_type_id = (SELECT id FROM inventory.material_type__t WHERE LOWER(name) = 'book' LIMIT 1). Do not JOIN material_type__t in the main query."
            ]
        },
        "inventory.holdings_record__t": {
            "preferredApproach": [
                "Use holdings_record__t as the bridge between instance and item; do not treat it as final location authority.",
